# PHP / Laravel Code Style

- Follow PSR-12 (spacing, braces, imports, visibility).
- Type-hint method params and return types; use `?Type` / unions where accurate.
- Prefer constructor property promotion for injected dependencies.
- Keep methods small and named after the business intent.
- Prefer query scopes / dedicated Actions over dumping filters in controllers.
- Eager load: `Model::with([...])->...` when relations are used in views/exports.
- Prefer `updateOrCreate`, mass assignment via `$fillable`/`$guarded`, and casts on models.
- Do not put authorization checks only in the UI; enforce in Policies/Form Requests.
- Prefer explicit exception messages useful for logs; do not swallow exceptions empty.
- When adding a module, place new business code under `app/Domain/{Module}/` first.
